# Pre-commit quality gate

Before creating any git commit in this repo:

1. Run `pnpm lint` (Biome) and fix all reported issues.
2. Run `pnpm typecheck` and fix all reported issues.
3. Only then stage and commit.

Do not skip these steps with `--no-verify`, `--no-hooks`, or by amending around a failed hook unless the user explicitly asks.

The git `pre-commit` hook runs `pnpm precommit` (`biome check --staged` + `pnpm typecheck`). Treat a hook failure as a hard stop: fix, then commit again.
